      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 5.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "ready for you, doctor i'll stay in case you need anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.05,
      "end_seconds": 11.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.1,
      "end_seconds": 17.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "I've, I've been dealing with pain in my right groin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 19.35,
      "end_seconds": 30.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "doctor I've got the readings for you. BP is 124 over 78 pulse is 66 beats a minute. Temperature 36.6 SpO2 99 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.36,
      "end_seconds": 35.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Okay, noted. When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.67,
      "end_seconds": 39.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "it's been going on for six months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.75,
      "end_seconds": 44.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.02,
      "end_seconds": 59.94,
      "duration_seconds": 13.92,
      "text": "Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. Yes, walking and stairs. That makes it worse. I've also had pain at night, for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.87,
      "end_seconds": 78.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "any fever, back pain or fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.24,
      "end_seconds": 84.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.13,
      "end_seconds": 90.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "a few quick ones: numbness in the leg or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.88,
      "end_seconds": 99.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "um, no, no numbness in the leg or weight loss"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.05,
      "end_seconds": 104.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Okay, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.77,
      "end_seconds": 108.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "no, uh, all normal there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.55,
      "end_seconds": 113.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.65,
      "end_seconds": 119.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "just keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.8,
      "end_seconds": 128.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine work habits that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.17,
      "end_seconds": 143.45,
      "duration_seconds": 13.28,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I walk the dog every morning. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.1,
      "end_seconds": 160.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.42,
      "end_seconds": 166.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "ah, you know, my father had bowel cancer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.18,
      "end_seconds": 172.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.71,
      "end_seconds": 188.16,
      "duration_seconds": 15.45,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes. I did try to ignore it it for a while. Yes, arthritis in my knees. I've been putting this off for weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.07,
      "end_seconds": 199.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "mm okay yes arthritis in your knees is known to us good to have that clear what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.93,
      "end_seconds": 205.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "yeah um I take paracetamol 650 milligrams when needed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.42,
      "end_seconds": 213.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "alright I'll need to examine you for this it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.84,
      "end_seconds": 216.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "raise your arm for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.13,
      "end_seconds": 233.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "Rotation of the right hip is painful and limited compared with the left"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.18,
      "end_seconds": 251.73,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "Alright, you can relax now. Putting it all together, this is probably osteoarthritis of the right hip. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.27,
      "end_seconds": 291.39,
      "duration_seconds": 31.12,
      "text": "let's book blood tests to look into joint pain. A hip X-ray is what I'd like next, for hip pain. Keep walking in short regular bursts and use a stick in the opposite hand. Losing even a few kilos takes a lot of load off the hip. I'm going to send a referral to physiotherapy. Let's get you seen by the orthopaedic clinic, I'll arrange the letter. Book a review after the X-ray"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.44,
      "end_seconds": 295.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "I can manage that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.72,
      "end_seconds": 301.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.34,
      "end_seconds": 306.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Okay that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.67,
      "end_seconds": 308.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
